# File: scripts/__tests__/sdlc-upgrade.test.mjs
# Generated from: specs/469-migrate-v3-oh-my-pi-references-and-move-agents-md-to-claude-md-during-sdlc-upgrade-project/requirements.md
Feature: Migrate v3 Oh My Pi references and move AGENTS.md to CLAUDE.md during /sdlc-upgrade-project

  @SCN001
  Scenario: Steering host tokens are proposed and rewritten
    Given a project whose registered snippets contain "omp --print", "--kind omp", "--kind pi", ".omp/sdlc/", "exercise-omp.mjs", "omp-sdlc-ignore.mjs", and "herdr integration install omp"
    And a manifest validation with program "omp" and args "--print" and "scripts/exercise-omp.mjs"
    When upgrade detect runs
    Then one actionable "steering-v4-host-language" item lists every occurrence with its exact before and after text
    And approved apply writes exactly the mapped replacements through the steering writer in update mode
    And the steering runtime validates afterward

  @SCN002
  Scenario: Steering host prose is proposed and rewritten
    Given a registered snippet containing "Oh My Pi", the whole word "OMP", the word "OMPX", and lowercase "omp"
    When the "steering-v4-host-language" group is approved
    Then "Oh My Pi" and "OMP" become "Claude Code"
    And "OMPX", lowercase "omp", and every other byte are unchanged

  @SCN003
  Scenario: v3 CONTRIBUTING.md wording is refreshed
    Given a CONTRIBUTING.md containing "drives Herdr omp worker panes through implementation, verification, and delivery" under a heading other than "nmg-sdlc Contribution Workflow"
    When upgrade detect runs and "contributing-v4-host-language" is approved
    Then the sentence becomes "drives Herdr Claude worker panes through implementation, verification, and delivery"
    And every other byte of the file is unchanged

  @SCN004
  Scenario: The new groups are idempotent and declinable
    Given a project where both groups were applied
    When upgrade detect runs again
    Then neither "steering-v4-host-language" nor "contributing-v4-host-language" is reported
    And a project whose approved ids exclude both groups keeps its steering and CONTRIBUTING.md bytes unchanged

  @SCN005
  Scenario: Unsafe or invalid steering fails closed
    Given a project with a mapped token and a registered snippet that is a symlink
    When apply runs for "steering-v4-host-language"
    Then the outcome is "skipped:unverifiable" with reason code "steering_host_language_unsafe_path" and no steering file changes
    And a project whose managed module was tampered with gets a "failed:" outcome with reason code "steering_module_invalid" and no steering file changes

  @SCN006
  Scenario: Documentation and this repository match the new groups
    Given this repository after the change
    When the upgrade documentation contract test runs
    Then the upgrade workflow, its v3-detectors, detection, and upgrade-procedures references, and README name all three groups
    And the contribution guide, project instructions contract, and onboarding workflow name CLAUDE.md
    And the repository has CLAUDE.md, has no AGENTS.md, and its .gitignore has no ".omp/sdlc/" rule

  @SCN007
  Scenario: AGENTS.md is renamed to CLAUDE.md
    Given a git-tracked regular root AGENTS.md and no CLAUDE.md
    When the "agents-to-claude-md" group is approved
    Then CLAUDE.md has the original AGENTS.md bytes
    And git records a rename from AGENTS.md to CLAUDE.md
    And no AGENTS.md remains

  @SCN008
  Scenario: AGENTS.md is merged into an existing CLAUDE.md
    Given regular root AGENTS.md and CLAUDE.md files that both contain the spec-context managed section
    When the "agents-to-claude-md" group is approved
    Then CLAUDE.md starts with its original bytes followed by one blank line and the AGENTS.md content
    And the spec-context managed section appears exactly once, as the copy from CLAUDE.md
    And AGENTS.md is deleted
    And a symlinked AGENTS.md instead reports "skipped:collision" with nothing changed

  @SCN009
  Scenario: Managed-section reconciliation uses CLAUDE.md
    Given a project with no AGENTS.md
    When the managed spec-context section is created or refreshed
    Then root CLAUDE.md holds the section and no AGENTS.md is created
    And a repeat upgrade detect reports no "agents-to-claude-md" item
